# Manga Gateway — example environment for docker compose.
#
# Copy to `.env` (git-ignored) and uncomment what you need:
#     cp .env.example .env
# All knobs are GATEWAY_-prefixed env vars (see src/manga_gateway/config.py).
# Precedence: env > TOML > default. The compose base file loads .env optionally,
# so the gateway also runs with NONE of these set (the image bakes safe defaults).
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# API KEY — DO NOT SET HERE.
# The API key is AUTO-GENERATED into the state volume's config.toml on first run
# (/state/config.toml) and logged once. Read it from there to authenticate
# (X-Api-Key header). GATEWAY_API_KEY is intentionally IGNORED (D-01) — setting
# it has no effect. Never put a real key in this file or commit a real .env.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Cloudflare / anti-bot engine ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Headless vs headed. true (default) = residential IP, no display needed.
# false = datacenter IP: Cloudflare fingerprints headless Chrome and blocks it;
# headed Chromium under Xvfb clears it. xvfb + fonts are ALREADY in the image,
# so headed works with NO image change — just flip this.
#GATEWAY_CLOUDFLARE_HEADLESS=true

# Engine. patchright (Chromium, default) runs Comix /search candidates in
# parallel. camoufox (Firefox) is the opt-in fallback for fingerprint-flagged
# hosts — but it is NOT baked into the image (LD-1); an operator using it must
# `camoufox fetch` at runtime AND pin GATEWAY_CLOUDFLARE_FETCH_CONCURRENCY=1
# (camoufox cannot run parallel — the app fails fast at startup otherwise, #64).
#GATEWAY_CLOUDFLARE_ENGINE=patchright

# Parallel browser navigations per /search. Default 3 (safe ONLY with
# engine=patchright). MUST be 1 when engine=camoufox.
#GATEWAY_CLOUDFLARE_FETCH_CONCURRENCY=3

# ── Single static residential proxy (PROXY-01, issue #65) ────────────────────
# Route both the stealth browser and the httpx image-fetch through one proxy so
# cf_clearance (IP-bound) and image fetches share an egress IP. An alternative to
# headed+Xvfb on a datacenter host.
#GATEWAY_CLOUDFLARE_PROXY_SERVER=http://host:port
#GATEWAY_CLOUDFLARE_PROXY_USERNAME=proxy-username
# SECRET — env-only. NEVER commit a real value; leave it in your local .env only.
#GATEWAY_CLOUDFLARE_PROXY_PASSWORD=
